---
/**
 * Metabolism — fourth biology-lens concept (Single Identity scale).
 * Process of the Cell: sustain, transform, prepare exchange.
 * Pedagogical order: Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Metabolism | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Single Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Metabolism
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					The continuous process of the Cell: transforming input into the maintenance of the form,
					the capacity to change, and the readiness to exchange with other living units.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: cellular metabolism / biochemistry of the living unit.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Pedagogical order:
						<a href="/framework/gene" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Gene</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/boundary" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Boundary</a>
						→
						<a href="/framework/cell" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Cell</a>
						→ Metabolism.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">How the unit keeps living.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, <strong class="text-white/85">metabolism</strong> is the set of transformations by which a living unit
					takes in material and energy, rebuilds and maintains itself, and releases waste or signals into its environment.
					It is not a separate organism. It is the process of the cell.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, <strong class="text-white/85">Metabolism</strong> names that process under the biology lens.
					After the Cell exists as a founded, bounded unit, Metabolism is how that unit
					<strong class="text-white/85">stays alive in time</strong>: converting Interaction and input into continued form,
					updated geometry, and the capacity to meet other cells without dissolving.
				</p>
				<p>
					Operationally this is close to Probes-as-Bridge and Geometry Receipt:
					Interaction enters under Boundary policy; the form transforms it into relative geometry;
					the living unit continues. Metabolism is the biology-lens name for that ongoing conversion.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Metabolism is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Process of the Cell:</strong> not a fourth free-floating substance, but what the living unit does continuously.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Maintenance under change:</strong> rebuild the form without erasing recognizability (continuity of Stem under update).
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Conversion of input into form-energy:</strong> experience, signal, resource, and constraint become structure, Mass, and option space when metabolized well.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge toward interaction:</strong> metabolism prepares export and import across the membrane.
						Without it, Boundary becomes a sealed tomb; with it, Signal and Coupling become possible.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Metabolism is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not the Cell.</strong>
						Cell is the living unit. Metabolism is its ongoing process.
						See <a href="/framework/cell" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Cell</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Boundary.</strong>
						Boundary decides what may cross. Metabolism transforms what has been admitted and prepares what may leave.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Gene.</strong>
						Gene founds. Metabolism runs after founding, inside the living unit.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not pure busyness.</strong>
						Activity without conversion into maintained form is leakage, not metabolism.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a claim of biochemical identity laws.</strong>
						Cellular metabolism is the science reading. The framework maps structure: continuous transformation that sustains a bounded form under Interaction.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Gene → Boundary → Cell → Metabolism</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-4 text-lg">
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Gene</strong> — founding core that can be passed.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Boundary</strong> — membrane that makes a distinct interior possible.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Cell</strong> — the living unit that is that founded, bounded form.</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Metabolism</strong> — the process by which the Cell sustains itself, transforms reality, and opens toward other cells.</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					With Metabolism, Single-scale biology-lens foundations are complete enough to move toward
					<strong class="text-white/85">Interactive</strong> concepts: Signal, Recognition, Coupling.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Convert, do not only consume:</strong> does Interaction become geometry and continuity, or only noise and exhaustion?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Keep Boundary and Metabolism paired:</strong> open enough to feed the process, closed enough to remain a form.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prefer living throughput over static purity:</strong> a sealed Identity cannot metabolize reality.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Use receipts as metabolic traces:</strong> in the OS, Geometry Receipts are local products of this conversion path.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">cellular metabolism / biochemistry</strong>
						(transformation networks that maintain the living unit under flux).
						Single-scale biology lens for this PR set ends here. Interactive scale (Signal, Recognition, Coupling) is next when we continue.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/gene" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Gene</a>
					<a href="/framework/boundary" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Boundary</a>
					<a href="/framework/cell" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Cell</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
